{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>And Moses came.</b> To indicate that after he went to each and every tribe and commanded them, upon his coming to the Tent of Meeting — and there all the children of Israel were assembled to him — then he spoke this song." "<b>He and Hosea son of Nun.</b> Like \"Then Moses sang and the children of Israel\" (Exodus 15:1) — this too, to elevate the stature of Joshua in the eyes of all. And Scripture calls him Hosea, by the name that all Israel knew him, for who knew that Moses had named him Joshua? Only those called to the meeting alone. And the way of derash is known."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:15.760765191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}